{
  "id": "29697_rikooru",
  "headword": "リコール",
  "reading": "りこーる",
  "romaji": "rikooru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "recall (of a defective product)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "recall (of a defective product)",
      "explanation": "A manufacturer's collection or free repair of products found to have a defect. As a suru-verb, リコールする means to recall such products."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "recall (of a public official)",
      "explanation": "A procedure by which voters remove an elected official or dissolve an assembly before the end of the term."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex1",
      "japanese": "その{車|くるま}はリコールになった。",
      "english": "That car was recalled.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex2",
      "japanese": "メーカーが{製品|せいひん}をリコールした。",
      "english": "The manufacturer recalled the product.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{不具合|ふぐあい}が{見|み}つかり、{大規模|だいきぼ}なリコールが{行|おこな}われた。",
      "english": "A defect was found, and a large-scale recall was carried out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{市長|しちょう}のリコールを{求|もと}める。",
      "english": "They are demanding the mayor's recall.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{住民|じゅうみん}がリコールの{署名|しょめい}を{集|あつ}めている。",
      "english": "Residents are collecting signatures for a recall.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29697_rikooru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{議会|ぎかい}の{解散|かいさん}を{求|もと}めるリコール{運動|うんどう}が{始|はじ}まった。",
      "english": "A recall campaign demanding the dissolution of the assembly has begun.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Loanword from English \"recall.\" By far the most common sense is a product recall (sense 1); the political sense (sense 2) appears mainly in news about local government.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- リコールになる: to be recalled\n- リコール{対象|たいしょう}: subject to a recall\n- リコールを{求|もと}める: to demand a recall (of an official)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {回収|かいしゅう}: collection, recall — the native term often used for gathering defective goods\n- {不具合|ふぐあい}: defect, malfunction — the problem that typically triggers a recall",
